lue "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d71b0cc6-29c4-5b34-b310-64ab60f5b724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545592} :answer-field/id #uuid "a810a855-c6d2-5045-a468-45c2987823ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545752}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e7c8be1-d271-506d-bfc9-fbf1881a88d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-142489" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1666c48c-616a-5584-b4b9-47f389d5edd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545240} {:answer/id #uuid "269226e3-2066-5e11-9e53-68cf25388793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545283} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab4711a-55c0-5e5e-90df-e23264046ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545478} {:answer/id #uuid "daf3c