er.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601729} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b6fd80-6441-5406-8fbe-9719cf74651a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9b6fd80-6441-5406-8fbe-9719cf74651a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601807} :answer-field/id #uuid "264078c2-360f-5a55-9a1d-47f10d85e767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601825}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7663d433-7983-5195-82f9-f8b3b6b0d6aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-79350" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186660860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ee71af-6ea0-54c0-b7a1-4d4f6222b4ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186660487} {:answer/id #uuid "6491a7a0-9bc2-5